---
const command = 'node /path/to/reviewed/notth/bin/aih.js init --host codex --adapters astro --capabilities uiux,product,architecture,delivery';
---
<section class="section install-section wrap" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
  <div class="install-intro"><p class="eyebrow">03 / START SMALL</p><h2 id="install-title">Your project.<br />A clearer path.</h2><p>Start with Core. Add only the support your project needs.</p><div class="prerequisite mono">NODE.JS 22+ <span>·</span> YOUR AI CODING TOOL</div><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/manh0303/notth/blob/main/docs/getting-started.md">Read the installation guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  <div class="install-panel">
    <div class="panel-heading"><span class="mono">SOURCE INSTALL / CODEX + ASTRO</span><span class="source-pill">Reviewed source</span></div>
    <ol class="install-steps"><li><span>01</span><p><a href="https://github.com/manh0303/notth/tree/11d662c9064cc989373e36b8c546cfb323a9b023">Download and review the source ↗</a><br /><small>Keep it outside your target project.</small></p></li><li><span>02</span><p>Open your project root.<br /><small>Replace the placeholder path below with your source location.</small></p></li></ol>
    <div class="command-box"><div class="command-toolbar"><span class="mono">TERMINAL</span><button class="copy-button" hidden>Copy command</button></div><pre><code id="install-command">{command}</code></pre><span class="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
    <div class="first-session"><span class="mono">03 / FIRST AI SESSION</span><p>“Read .agents/skills/harness-start/SKILL.md and follow it for this project. My task: [task].”</p></div>
    <p class="install-note">Registry check · 15 Oct 2026: npm returned E404. This preview uses the official source installation path.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<script>
  const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.copy-button');
  const code = document.querySelector('#install-command');
  const status = document.querySelector('.copy-status');
  if (button && code && status) {
    button.hidden = false;
    button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent ?? ''); status.textContent = 'Command copied. Replace the placeholder path before running.'; }
      catch { status.textContent = 'Copy unavailable. Select and copy the command manually.'; }
    });
  }
</script>
